==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{affix|la|in|nuce}}, the ablative singular of {{m|la|nux|t=nut}}: {{lit|in a nut|nocap=1}}. Derived from an anecdote in {{w|Pliny the Elder}}, who ascribes to {{w|Cicero}} the claim that the whole ''{{w|Iliad}}'' was once written on parchment and enclosed within a nutshell (''{{w|Naturalis Historia}}'' [[wikisource:la:Naturalis Historia/Liber VII#XXI|7.21.85]]).

===Adverb===
{{la-adv|[[in]] [[nux|nuce]]|-}} {{tlb|la|New Latin}}

